=== MUTATION TESTING ===
32 mutations across orchestration.py and enums.py.
31 killed, 1 survivor, 0 inapplicable. Sources restored byte-identical.

Two survived the first pass:
  M15 serialised phases dispatched in parallel too  -> EQUIVALENT MUTANT
  M18 worker results not guarded by the lock        -> now killed

M15 is provably equivalent and remains a survivor by design. ExecutionPhase
refuses a multi-item serialised phase at construction, so `len(admitted) > 1`
is unreachable for a serialised phase and the `phase.is_parallel` conjunct
cannot change behaviour. The redundant guard is retained because it states the
N-11 intent at the point of dispatch. Demonstrated by
TestEquivalentMutantGuards::test_a_serialised_phase_can_never_hold_more_than_one_item.

M18 survived because dict assignment and list.extend are atomic under CPython's
GIL, so its removal is unobservable on this interpreter. The lock is required
on a free-threaded build, so its presence is now asserted directly.

