=== DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED ===

BOUNDED CONCURRENT PHASE STARVED THE WHOLE CYCLE.
Phase admission was all-or-nothing: a phase whose size exceeded the remaining
work budget was refused entire. A work set of 12 acquisition items forms ONE
concurrent phase, so under max_work_items=4 the parallel path attempted ZERO
items while the sequential path attempted 4. Starvation is a named Orchestration
failure mode (PKP v2 4.12), and the divergence meant concurrency silently
changed how much work a bounded cycle performed -- which N-11 must never do.
Root cause: the bound counts WORK, not phases. Fixed by admitting the prefix of
a phase that fits the remaining budget, which is exactly the work the sequential
path would have run. Sequential and parallel now agree at every limit, verified
exhaustively for limits 1..13 and by property test over random bounds.

=== SPECIFICATION NOTES ===
No document conflicts found. N-11, IOM 2.6, R-1, N-17 and B-09 agree on every
point binding this task.

Ambiguity A1 (the instruction to "preserve deterministic behaviour" versus N-4,
which guarantees reproducible INPUTS but explicitly not deterministic OUTPUTS)
was resolved in favour of the ratified decision: determinism is enforced in
every respect the platform controls -- recorded invocation order is always
work-set order regardless of thread completion order, results are reassembled
by index, and bounds apply deterministically. Engine outputs remain
non-deterministic per N-4, which this task does not change.
